  "worked_solution": "First, we write down the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 6 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -6-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}|=0 \\\\ -\\lambda |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ -3 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|=0 \\\\ \\lambda ((3-\\lambda )(-6-\\lambda )+18)=0 \\\\ \\lambda (-18+3\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+18)=0 \\\\ \\lambda (3\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2})=0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}(3+\\lambda )=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=0$ (double root) and ${\\lambda }_{3}=-3$ (simple root).\n\nLet's now consider the eigenspaces corresponding to each eigenvector:\n\n- First, we consider $\\lambda =-3.$ Since ${V}_{-3}$ corresponds to a simple root, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({V}_{-3})=1.\n$$\n\n- Then, we consider $\\lambda =0,$ which is a repeated root of the characteristic equation. To find the dimension of ${V}_{0},$ we row-reduce the matrix $(A-0I)\\text{x}=0:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}]-0[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). This implies that we will have $3-1=2$ linearly independent eigenvectors corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =0.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({V}_{0})=2.\n$$",
